# HTML Structure

All HTML files must follow regional organization and 4-space indentation.

## Regional Structure

```html
<!-- #Region ------------------------------------------ -->
<!-- BLOCK TYPE | Section Description                  -->
<!-- -------------------------------------------------- -->

    <!-- Content (4-space indent) -->

<!-- endregion ---------------------------------------- -->
```

**Common Regions:** Document Head, Document Body, JavaScript Modules

**Component Types:** UI HEADER, UI NAVIGATION, UI MAIN CONTENT, UI SECTION, UI SIDEBAR, UI MODAL, UI FOOTER

**Dash Counts:** Opening (65), Subsection (57 with indent), Closing (60)

---

## Required Head Structure

```html
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <meta name="description" content="Application description">
    <meta name="author" content="Adam Noble - Noble Architecture">
    
    <title>Page Title - Noble Architecture</title>
    
    <!-- Favicons: Use data-asset-href attribute for AssetLoader -->
    <link rel="icon" data-asset-href="../../01__Assets__NaApps__CommonAssets/NaApps__CommonIcons/CommonIcon__NaFavicon__ICO-h32px.ico">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="StyleSheet__Main__.css">
</head>
```

**Note:** Favicon paths use `data-asset-href` attributes instead of `href`. The `AssetLoader` module parses these data attributes on initialization and injects absolute GitHub Pages URLs, preventing 404 errors before the app fully loads.

---

## Semantic Elements

Use semantic HTML5 elements: `<header>`, `<nav>`, `<main>`, `<article>`, `<section>`, `<aside>`, `<footer>`

```html
<header class="app-header">
    <nav class="main-navigation">
        <ul class="nav-list">
            <li><a href="#">Link</a></li>
        </ul>
    </nav>
</header>

<main class="app-content">
    <section class="content-section">
        <h2>Section Title</h2>
    </section>
</main>
```

---

## Accessibility

```html
<button aria-label="Close dialog" class="close-button">×</button>
<nav role="navigation" aria-label="Main navigation"></nav>
<label for="project-code">Project Code:</label>
<input id="project-code" aria-required="true">
```

---

## ID & Class Naming

**IDs:** kebab-case, descriptive, unique
```html
<div id="project-admin-container">
    <div id="project-list-section">
```

**Classes:** kebab-case, BEM-style
```html
<div class="project-card project-card--featured">
    <div class="project-card__header">
        <h3 class="project-card__title">Title</h3>
```

---

## Script Loading Order

```html
<!-- #Region ------------------------------------------ -->
<!-- REGION | JavaScript Modules                       -->
<!-- -------------------------------------------------- -->
    <!-- 1. Module Dependency Manager (FIRST) -->
    <script src="03__Src__AppModules/01__AppCore/AppCore__ModuleDependencyManager__.js"></script>
    
    <!-- 2. Configuration Manager -->
    <script src="03__Src__AppModules/01__AppCore/AppCore__ConfigManager__.js"></script>
    
    <!-- 3. Common Utilities (including AssetLoader) -->
    <script src="03__Src__AppModules/03__CommonUtils/CommonUtils__ProjectCodeValidator__.js"></script>
    <script src="03__Src__AppModules/03__CommonUtils/CommonUtils__DateFormatter__.js"></script>
    <script src="03__Src__AppModules/03__CommonUtils/CommonUtils__AssetLoader__.js"></script>
    
    <!-- 4. User Interface Modules -->
    <script src="03__Src__AppModules/10__UserInterface/UserInterface__Navigation__.js"></script>
    
    <!-- 5. Feature Modules -->
    <script src="03__Src__AppModules/20__DocumentSystem/DocumentSystem__QuotationRenderer__.js"></script>
    
    <!-- 6. Main Application Entry Point (LAST) -->
    <script src="03__Src__AppModules/01__AppCore/AppCore__Main__.js"></script>
<!-- endregion ---------------------------------------- -->
```

**Critical:** `AssetLoader` must be loaded after `ConfigManager` but before any modules that reference assets.

---

## Rules

### ALWAYS
- Use regional organization with proper dividers
- Use 4-space indentation consistently
- Use semantic HTML5 elements
- Include proper meta tags in head
- Load ModuleDependencyManager first
- Include ARIA labels for accessibility
- Close regions with `endregion`
- Use descriptive IDs (kebab-case) and BEM classes

### NEVER
- Use tabs instead of spaces
- Skip regional organization
- Use generic divs when semantic elements exist
- Forget accessibility attributes
- Load scripts in wrong order
- Use inline styles
- Omit alt text for images
